    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$3 \\alpha=\\frac{1-3 a}{a^2-5 a+3} \\& 2 \\alpha^2=\\frac{2}{a^2-5 a+3}$\n$2\\left[\\frac{1}{9} \\frac{(1-3 a)^2}{\\left(a^2-5 a+3\\right)^2}\\right]=\\frac{2}{a^2-5 a+3}$\n$\\frac{(1-3 a)^2}{\\left(a^2-5 a+3\\right)}=9$ or $9 a^2-6 a+1$\n$=9 a^2-45 a+27$ or $39 a=26$ or $a=\\frac{2}{3}$"
  }
